 "notes": [
  "Timings (verify_ms, propose_ms) assume the machine is otherwise idle (run overnight); if something else was running on the machine they may be noisy.",
  "bf16 ulp gap: round both values to bfloat16, reinterpret the 16-bit pattern as an order-preserving unsigned integer (the standard radix-sort-floats sign-flip trick), and take the absolute difference of those integers. gap(1.0, next bf16 above 1.0) == 1; gap(x, x) == 0.",
  "Equivalence recompute at a divergence: for a divergence at the very first generated token (index 0), all three paths' first token came from a single one-shot forward over the whole prompt, so the recompute uses that same one-shot batch for every path. For a later divergence, each path's own steady-state batching is replayed instead: a single-token decode step (batch size 1) for std/trim, an (n_draft+1)-token block for dflash. Both sides use the same target weights and the same token history, so any gap tests whether batched-vs-single matmul reduction order changes the result, not a model difference.",
  "Single run per target; no repeats for Part A (equivalence is exact-match, not a noisy metric)."
 ]
